The main change replaces the equality-based conditional partition with a bounded greedy cross-row pairing construction. It searches for pairs of rows whose values have long textual prefixes even when those values come from different columns, assigns each paired row an appropriate leading column, and fills the remainder using the global frequency order. The candidate is still evaluated with the exact sorted serialized-row LCP objective, so it competes fairly with the two global candidates.

